import json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]; x=json.loads((root/'evaluation/framework_upstream_audit.json').read_text()); related=json.loads((root/'evaluation/framework_related_changes.json').read_text())
lines=['# Framework version audit — 2026-10-10 UTC','','Read-only official GitHub API and PyPI queries; raw responses: `evaluation/framework_upstream_audit.json`, `framework_related_changes.json`. No repository checkout or Python package upgrades performed.','', '| Framework | Current | Latest official release / commit | Decision |','|---|---|---|---|']
for name in ['Isaac-GR00T','RoboTwin','XPolicyLab','LeRobot']:
 v=x[name]; rel=v['latest_release']; tags=v['tags']; desc='No published release or tags' if 'error' in rel else f"{rel['tag_name']} ({rel['published_at']}); tag commit "+ next((t['commit']['sha'] for t in tags if t['name']==rel['tag_name']),'unresolved')
 current=v.get('local_commit','installed LeRobot 0.3.3; no independent LeRobot Git checkout')
 decision={'Isaac-GR00T':'Keep: local equals latest main HEAD; N1.7 checkpoint loads. Tagged release is Early Access, not a newer fix.','RoboTwin':'Keep: local equals latest main HEAD; official expert replay succeeds.','XPolicyLab':'Keep pinned RoboTwin submodule; latest changes are not a validated migration for this checkpoint.','LeRobot':'Keep conversion baseline 0.3.3/v2.1. Trial 0.6.1 only in a separate environment; v3 data and new policy/processor APIs need migration tests.'}[name]
 lines.append(f"| {name} | `{current}` | {desc} | {decision} |")
lines+=['','## Main branch inventory','']
for name in ['Isaac-GR00T','RoboTwin','XPolicyLab','LeRobot']:
 v=x[name]; c=v['latest_commit'][0]; lines.append(f"- {name}: [{c['sha']}]({c['url']}) — {c['date']}; {c['message'].splitlines()[0]}.")
lines+=['','## Verified changes and known issues','','- Isaac-GR00T already includes the July 29 inference image-path change (`238ef45`), June shard-loading fix (`026af18`), and action-horizon validation fix (`376ba89`). Current main is N1.7; no model family switch is needed. The separately announced N1.7 General Release is commit `1a1837f205` (2026-07-07); the latest GitHub release tag remains the older Early Access tag. Main branch commits are not automatically stable releases. [Official history](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/commits/main/)','- RoboTwin already includes reproducible episode/model enumeration fixes (#509/#490), joint-limit checking (`bd56368`) and codec synchronization. These improve reproducibility and image correctness; they do not certify policy success. [Official history](https://github.com/RoboTwin-Platform/RoboTwin/commits/main/)','- XPolicyLab RGB handling was unified by [`66ecde3`](https://github.com/XPolicyLab/XPolicyLab/commit/66ecde3ed34a83e4de56c7a36a3e81fe29f093ec), 2026-08-04; adapter/converter audit completed by [`14bb308`](https://github.com/XPolicyLab/XPolicyLab/commit/14bb3081611b093227b3cd3262bb72d39824161a), 2026-09-10. Both precede the pinned submodule. The project’s own historical conversion still added an extra swap, so an upstream update cannot repair existing videos/checkpoints.','- [N1.7 issue #742](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/issues/742): padded action noise may affect valid predictions. [PR #741](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/pull/741) is OPEN and unmerged at audit time. Applying a new mask only at inference changes the distribution for existing weights; no unverified patch applied. This is a potential mechanism, not a demonstrated cause here.','- [Issue #745](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/issues/745) concerns the unused `use_mean_std` flag. This checkpoint sets it false; actions use recorded percentile/min-max statistics. No evidence that this issue caused the observed failures.','- [Issue #546](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/issues/546) and [official data configuration](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/getting_started/data_config.md): changing model action horizon requires matching relative statistics. We keep prediction horizon 40 and only change the executed prefix.','- [LeRobot v0.6.1](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/releases/tag/v0.6.1), 2026-08-03, supports updated N1.7 integration, but includes a module rename and follows the v3 dataset migration. It is not a drop-in replacement for NVIDIA Gr00tPolicy checkpoints and this v2.1 converter.','', '## SAPIEN and actual environment','','- SAPIEN installed: 3.0.0b1; latest PyPI stable: 3.0.3, uploaded 2026-03-10. Official 3.0.3 tag maps to `731622eac5b140b320076c8a1b6eb4b553c3ccd4`; binary wheel provenance is not independently attested. Official tag mapping is recorded in `framework_related_changes.json`. [Official docs](https://sapien-sim.github.io/docs/), [PyPI metadata](https://pypi.org/pypi/sapien/json), [source tags](https://github.com/haosulab/SAPIEN/tags).','- Keep 3.0.0b1 for the recovery baseline because it is the RoboTwin pinned requirement and expert physics replay passes. 3.0.3 must first pass scene, camera, planner, drive and expert-replay comparisons in an isolated environment; physics changes can alter grasp contact outcomes.','- Existing GR00T: Python 3.12 / torch 2.9.0+cu128 / transformers 4.57.3 / numpy 1.26.4 / pyarrow 20.0.0 / flash-attn 2.8.3. Simulation: Python 3.10 / torch 2.4.1 / SAPIEN 3.0.0b1. Conversion: LeRobot 0.3.3 / pyarrow 25.0.1. Actual metadata captured in `configs/recovery_*_versions.json`.','- Container recreation removed EGL/GL user libraries although persistent virtualenvs survived. Restored only container user libraries `libegl1 libgl1 libglvnd0 vulkan-tools`; SAPIEN now creates a renderer and executes the official task. No Python environment overwritten.','','## Storage and checkpoint preservation','','- `/`: overlay Container Disk, 650GB, temporary container storage. `/workspace`: `mfs#eu-se-1.runpod.net:9421` FUSE network volume, separate mount. Project artifacts survived this recreation. This supports persistence across the observed recreation, not a guarantee of retention after volume deletion.','- `df` 756TB/235TB is shared backend capacity. No `quota` utility/account quota endpoint is available in this session; precise personal quota remains UNVERIFIED. Do not infer it from backend free space.','- Existing checkpoint/data/videos preserved. No external backup destination configured. Header validation and configuration hashes recorded in `evaluation/recovery_asset_audit.json`; checkpoint tensor offsets and shard index agree. Full model reload is tested by actual inference.','','## Project-specific sampling finding\n\nLatest official main retains `length - action_horizon + 1` observation sampling. On this short Lift Pot dataset with horizon 40, this excludes 1560 real training observations and all 990 closed-gripper states. Merely upgrading dependencies or toggling allow_padding does not restore that sampler range. Verified training-only terminal future-target padding in a new dataset restores all 4444 real observations without modifying baseline upstream code. See `evaluation/training_tail_coverage_audit.json` and `terminal_pad_sampler_check.json`. [Official sampler](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/gr00t/data/dataset/sharded_single_step_dataset.py).\n\n## Migration acceptance criteria','','Use a separate environment/checkouts; preserve all baseline artifacts. Require unchanged checkpoint tensor loading, processor/statistics and 14-dimensional action mapping; identical golden-observation preprocessing and decoded actions; expert replay success; then fixed-seed real-model evaluation. Recompute statistics only for a new dataset/config version. Do not change N1.7 model family or reinterpret joint targets as EEF deltas.']
(root/'results/framework_version_audit.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
